>> title: Bigotes de Piña
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, mexican, pineapple, sweet, oven
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: bigote, bigotes, bigote de pina, bigote de piña, moustache roll, mustache roll, pan bigote
>> pairs-with: pan-dulce-dough, relleno-de-pina, costra-de-azucar
>> servings: 12
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> step.1: roll and cut 12 rectangles
>> step.2: pipe the filling and roll up
>> step.3: shape into moustaches, proof 60 min
>> step.4: pipe on the paste, wash and bake at 350°F 18 min

Roll @masa para pan dulce{800%g}(three-quarters of a batch, chilled) to a 1/4-inch sheet on a bench dusted with @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(16 g) and cut 12 rectangles of about 4 by 5 inches.

Pipe @relleno de piña{300%g}(half a batch, cold) in a line down each of @&(~1)rectangles{} and roll them up into tight logs, sealing the seam.

Lay @&(~1)filled logs{} seam down on trays greased with @vegetable shortening{1%Tbs}(14 g), bend each into a shallow curve with the ends drawn down, and ~proof{60%min}. The curve is the name and the only reason to tell it apart from a rol.

Pipe three stripes of @costra de azúcar{200%g}(half a batch, plain) along the back of @&(~1)proofed bigotes{}, brush the bare dough with @beaten egg{1%large}(50 g), and bake at 350°F for ~bake{18%min}.
